Here is the commit message:
SOLR-9549: Fix bug in advancing docValues

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from using the wrong document ID as an argument in the `advance` method, which prevents the correct advancement to the appropriate document value, potentially leading to incorrect or incomplete data retrieval during the execution of the `collect` method.

Here is the patch:

     public void collect(int doc) throws IOException{
       int valuesDocID = leafOutcomeValue.docID();
       if (valuesDocID < doc) {
-        valuesDocID = leafOutcomeValue.advance(valuesDocID);
+        valuesDocID = leafOutcomeValue.advance(doc);
       }
       int outcome;
       if (valuesDocID == doc) {
         outcome = (int) leafOutcomeValue.longValue();
       } else {
         outcome = 0;
       }

       outcome = trainingParams.positiveLabel == outcome? 1 : 0;
       if (outcome == 1) {
         positiveDocsSet.set(context.docBase + doc);
       }
       docsSet.set(context.docBase+doc);

     }



